From: Radical <radical@radical.fun>
Subject: [PATCH] drm: wait for the lock state before lighting the companion

The lock atom only arrives once Steam and armada-control are up, so the
companion was usable until then, including past a lock screen Steam shows
on start. With GAMESCOPE_COMPANION_WAIT_FOR_LOCK=1 it starts locked and
follows the atom from its first value.
---
diff --git a/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp b/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp
index a857f05..194eba2 100644
--- a/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp
+++ b/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp
@@ -1661,7 +1661,8 @@ static bool g_bLeaseClientYields = false;
 static bool g_bLeaseClientSuspendPending = false;
 static bool g_bLeaseClientSuspended = false;
 static uint64_t g_uLeaseClientGeneration = 0;
-static bool g_bLeaseCompanionLocked = false;
+// Keep the companion locked until the first GAMESCOPE_COMPANION_LOCKED value arrives.
+static bool g_bLeaseCompanionLocked = getenv( "GAMESCOPE_COMPANION_WAIT_FOR_LOCK" ) && !strcmp( getenv( "GAMESCOPE_COMPANION_WAIT_FOR_LOCK" ), "1" );
 static bool g_bLeaseCompanionAsleep = false;
 
 extern gamescope::ConVar<bool> cv_drm_sleep_screens[];
